            "review_title": "Review at Gammer Beer",
            "review_text": "Anna S\nMalaysia1137 contributions\n0\nBeer and service were excellent and the audience was Asian on both nights. We felt very comfortable.\nFeb 2025 • Couples\nImpressive restaurant on a slightly elevated covered terrace on the very pleasant tree-lined Pasteur Street.\nYou have to go up a few steps and then you see a very large and very friendly hall. Almost a beer garden milieu from which you have a beautiful view over the street. A mega screen where you could have watched football from GB didn't fit. We sat with our backs to this wall.\nWe stayed here two nights and drank only beer here. The latter was quite excellent. It came on tap, served in glass jugs, was well tapped and tasted quite excellent. The price was also moderate. The food was not expensive either, but the offer here was too strong European for us; we saw mountains of French fries. We love country cuisine on all our trips.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from German\nShow original\nWritten May 22, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
